          "message": "Likely layout problem on mobile, read in the code but not rendered. In the card view, the 'failed' and 'avg duration' cells (StatsPage.tsx:79-86) are `display:flex; justify-content:space-between` (components.css:314-320), and each holds three items: the label from ::before, the value as an anonymous text item, and the .meter. With space-between, the value ends up centred and the meter pinned to the right edge, instead of the value and meter sitting together on the right. The new `display:inline-block` does nothing here, because the meter is a flex item. Fix: in the same media query, add `.table-wrap[data-variant=\"cards\"] td::before { margin-right: auto; }`. The auto margin overrides space-between and groups the value and meter on the right. Keep the meter's `margin-left: var(--space-2)`."
